  "chordFingerings": {
    "G": "Partial G: middle finger on low E fret 3, ring finger on high E fret 3; G and B open. Do not play A or D."
  },
  "lesson": {
    "instructions": "Count 1-and-2-and-3-and. Pluck bass, G, B, G, high E, B as six even eighth notes: p-i-m-i-a-m. Thumb p plays the bass; i plays G, m plays B and a plays high E. Each note is separate; do not pinch two strings together. Partial G: middle finger on low E fret 3, ring finger on high E fret 3; G and B open. Do not play A or D. Play two bars, then rest for one bar. Repeat three times. This is a new picking order after Quiet Morning; learn it without changing the left hand.",
